hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"186","This is Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb, this is Abu Usama. H. Salam bin Junada, na Waki’, both of them, told us on the authority of Al-A’mash. H Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Al-A’mash narrated to us. Al-Sana'ani narrated to us, Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, narrated to us Shu'bah, on the authority of Suleiman, who is Al-A'mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, he said: I saw Jarir urinated, then called for water. He performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then he stood up and prayed. He was asked about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he did something like this.” This is the hadith of al-San’aani, and the others did not say: I saw Jarir. In the hadith of Abu Usama, Ibrahim said: Our companions liked the hadith of Jarir, because his conversion to Islam occurred after the revelation of the Messenger of Allah. And in the hadith of Waki`: They liked the hadith of Jarir. He converted to Islam after the revelation of the Messenger of Allah."
"187","On the authority of Abu Ammar Al-Hussein bin Harith, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Bukayr bin Amir Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, that Jarir urinated, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks. They criticized him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “wiping over his socks.” It was said to him: Is that before the table? He said: “My conversion to Islam occurred after the table.”"
"188","It is narrated by Abu Muhammad Fahd bin Sulaiman Al-Basri, it is narrated by Musa bin Dawud, it is narrated by Hafs bin Ghayath, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, On the authority of Jarir bin Abdullah, he said: “I converted to Islam forty days before the death of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
